==Spanish==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{der|es|VL.|*cattulus|t=whelp, puppy}}, from {{der|es|la|catŭlus|t=puppy}}.<ref>{{R:es:DRAE}}</ref><ref>{{R:es:Roberts:2014}}</ref><ref>{{R:pt:DAN|cachorro}}</ref>

Or, from or influenced by a metathesis of {{der|es|eu|txakur}}, {{m|eu|xakur||puppy}};<ref>Spanish in Contact: Issues in Bilingualism. (1996). United States: Cascadilla Press, p. 3</ref> however, this has been dismissed as speculative.<ref>Trask, R. L. (2013). The History of Basque. United Kingdom: Taylor & Francis, p. 416</ref> Compare with {{cog|it|cucciolo}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m|f=+}}

# [[puppy]]
#: {{syn|es|perrito}}
# [[cub]] {{gloss|the young of certain other animals, generally mammals}}
# [[pup]] {{gloss|young of foxes, seals or sea lions}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|es|cachorro de [[lobo]]}} (wolf cub, wolfling)
* {{l|es|Cachorros de Chicago||Chicago Cubs}}

